5 since 1892, the coolest since 2022. The normal high for the date is 60\u00b0F, and the record is 82\u00b0F (1955). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Harrison has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Harrison's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Harrison has set <strong class=\"sig\">13 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 80 that chance alone would give, and <strong>56 record highs</strong>, fewer than the 80 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (70). Harrison's all-time high is 112\u00b0F, on August 9, 1934.","t_chg":"Harrison's nights warmed over the long run. Its days cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 103 complete years: Harrison's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.44\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.36 to +0.53), about +5.5\u00b0F since 1901. Harrison's average high has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.26 to \u22120.05), about \u22121.9\u00b0F since 1901. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows show no clear change and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.47\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.06 to +0.88). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in none; 6 months fell.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Harrison's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.31 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 44.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1945 (66.45 in); the driest, 1963 (24.67 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}